Vendoring provenance and licence — cockpit-contract schemas
================================================================

Scope: every JSON Schema file under `schema/` in this directory (the vendored
Cockpit-contract bundle). This LICENSE file itself is not part of the
vendored bundle and is not covered by it — it is the provenance record
describing it.

What this is
------------
The schemas under `schema/` are vendored (copied, not generated in this
repository) from a private upstream repository, where they are frozen and
versioned independently. They are not independently authored or maintained
in this repository.

The rights-holder on both the upstream repository and this one is the same
party. Because the rights-holder on both sides is identical, this file
constitutes a self-issued licence grant covering the vendored bundle's
inclusion here — not a grant obtained from an unaffiliated third party.

Licence terms
-------------
The vendored schema files are licensed under: **Apache License 2.0, modified
by the Commons Clause**.

This is a SOURCE-AVAILABLE licence, not an open-source licence — the Commons
Clause restricts the right to "Sell" the software as defined in that clause.
This published release carries this same combined licence at its own
repository root, naming this vendored bundle's inclusion under identical
terms. Nothing in this file grants broader rights over the vendored schemas
than that combined licence grants over the rest of this release.

Regenerating this bundle
-------------------------
The files under `schema/` here are a vendored, frozen copy consumed by this
engine's own validators; they are not independently authored or maintained
in this repository. The canonical generator for this bundle is an equivalent
of this engine's own `contract.cockpit_schema.emit_schema` (see
`coordinator_core/contract/cockpit_schema.py` for the consuming side) —
upstream, that generator is the single process that produces these schemas'
bytes.
